    <briefdescription>
<para>The pool for deliberately slow password work (hashing and verification), so it never runs on a Drogon IO thread. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Keeping password operations off the IO threads prevents them from blocking request handling. Queueing, fair dispatch, zero-worker inline mode and shutdown semantics are inherited from BoundedExecutor; see that class for the queue and inline-mode rules. Think of it as a queue with a fixed number of helpers: requests drop a job in the queue, and a free helper picks it up. <simplesect kind="see"><para>BoundedExecutor, <ref refid="passwordworker_8hpp_1a11301e300507b2f5ba81930e709a5de6" kindref="member">runOnPasswordWorker</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
